---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Reports · Eleven One Research"
  description="Three ways to buy the work: packaged reports, briefed studies against a written brief, and bespoke engagements."
  current="reports"
>
  <Prose
    title="Reports"
    standfirst="Three ways to buy the work. The briefs are free and always will be. These are what the briefs are meant to earn."
  >
    <div class="tier">
      <h3>Reports</h3>
      <p>Packaged sector intelligence, written once and sold as it is. Nothing is gated: no email wall, no registration, no preview that stops at the interesting part. You see what you are buying before you buy it.</p>
      <p class="status">Pricing is not set. When it is, it will be on this page rather than behind a conversation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tier">
      <h3>Briefed studies</h3>
      <p>Custom research produced against a written brief. You write down the question, we write down what would answer it, and the scope is fixed before any work starts. The deliverable carries the same apparatus a published brief carries: sources, assumptions and falsifiers on the page.</p>
      <p class="status">Scope and turnaround are agreed per study.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tier">
      <h3>Engagements</h3>
      <p>Bespoke diligence and analysis, scoped per client. This is the tier for questions that will not fit in a document written in advance: a live deal, a board question with a date on it, a competitive response that has to be right the first time.</p>
      <p class="status">Scoped on the question. There is no rate card for this tier.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>How buying works</h2>
    <p>A buyer should be able to evaluate the work and decide without a meeting. That is why briefs are published in full: the work is the argument for the work, and judging it costs nothing. A conversation comes after that, if you want one.</p>
    <p>There is no list to join on this site and no sequence to be dropped into.</p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
